    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1087">

                <pb facs="1013" n="755" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg755"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in France</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Sharp</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-12-28T15:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 28, 1915, 3 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1283. Your 1179, December 27. If opportunity presents itself please convey to
                    Foreign Minister that even if, as he supposed, men were removed from steamers on
                    account of suspicion German plots and intrigues in the West Indies, this is not
                    regarded by the Department as justification for the seizure of the men and that
                    even if the men were found to be implicated in such plots and intrigues, they
                    could not, in the view of the Department, be rightfully detained on that
                    account.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
